# A set member registers its catalog row as soon as it is captured, and the
# stamp registers it again, as production did before #5449. Between the two
# a retention pass can prune the member, and the stamp lists it again over
# its deleted artifact. Stamp(c) is the member's only registration.
MODULE: BackupRetention
ROW: Stamp(c)
FILE: src/lattice.backup/LatticeBackupCaptureService.cs
DETECTORS: BackupRetentionConcurrencyTests.A_pass_during_a_set_capture_does_not_leave_a_member_listed_over_a_deleted_artifact
SUMMARY: a set member is listed before the stamp, so a pass can prune it and the stamp re-lists it

--- FIND
                        request.Name, scope, request.PageSize, cancellationToken, register: !deferRegistration)
--- REPLACE
                        request.Name, scope, request.PageSize, cancellationToken, register: true)
--- END
